WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.520
Good to have you on Tesla's short time, Daily, Episode 510 for June 14th, 2026.

00:00:06.260 --> 00:00:08.000
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver.

00:00:08.580 --> 00:00:10.240
Here's what's happening with Tesla today.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:16.360
The week's biggest developments pulled together what actually moved, why it matters, and what to watch next.

00:00:17.140 --> 00:00:22.740
Goldman Sachs added 1.98 million shares of Tesla in the first quarter of 2026.

00:00:23.520 --> 00:00:28.200
The bank had trimmed holdings by $1.4 billion in the prior two quarters.

00:00:28.920 --> 00:00:34.920
Its current position sits at 29.4 million shares valued at $10.93 billion.

00:00:35.880 --> 00:00:41.200
Goldman is also serving as lead underwriter for the planned SpaceX initial public offering.

00:00:42.000 --> 00:00:47.520
The shift comes amid ongoing questions about Tesla's valuation and institutional ownership trends,

00:00:47.940 --> 00:00:52.140
from Wall Street positioning to the operational results that likely influenced it.

00:00:52.700 --> 00:00:57.960
Tesla China retail sales reached 47,281 vehicles in May.

00:00:58.560 --> 00:01:03.340
That figure marked a 22.53% increase from the same month last year.

00:01:04.000 --> 00:01:10.780
Exports from the Shanghai factory climbed 67.73% to 38,701 units.

00:01:11.240 --> 00:01:15.280
The rebound ends two consecutive months of sales declines in the region.

00:01:16.020 --> 00:01:20.380
Giga Shanghai continues to balance domestic deliveries with exports to other markets.

00:01:21.100 --> 00:01:25.780
Sales momentum in China pairs with infrastructure moves that support long-term growth there.

00:01:26.360 --> 00:01:30.300
Tesla is shipping its first foldable supercharger units to Europe.

00:01:30.940 --> 00:01:36.000
The portable design is intended to accelerate site construction compared with fixed stations.

00:01:36.620 --> 00:01:41.540
European supercharger expansion has lagged behind North American growth in recent quarters.

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:47.240
Faster deployment could help prepare the network for wider use of supervised full self-driving.

00:01:47.880 --> 00:01:52.160
The first European sites using the new hardware are expected in the coming months.

00:01:52.780 --> 00:01:57.180
Hardware expansion on the ground connects to software progress on the vehicle side.

00:01:57.940 --> 00:02:03.360
Tesla CyberCab vehicles have now been documented in 16 states plus Washington, DC.

00:02:04.140 --> 00:02:09.720
Sighting span coastal states such as California and New York, as well as central states including

00:02:09.720 --> 00:02:16.640
Missouri and Oklahoma. The testing activity covers both urban and highway environments across diverse regions.

00:02:17.240 --> 00:02:22.420
This broad footprint reflects ongoing work toward unsupervised operation capability.

00:02:23.300 --> 00:02:27.660
Regulators in multiple jurisdictions will review data from these varied locations.

00:02:28.500 --> 00:02:33.680
Real-world testing volume leads into how the supervised system is being defended today.

00:02:34.520 --> 00:02:39.660
Tesla released its first localized full self-driving safety snapshot for the Netherlands.

00:02:40.280 --> 00:02:45.540
The report focuses on roundabout navigation and right-of-way performance in local conditions.

00:02:46.260 --> 00:02:51.100
This marks an early effort to supply region-specific metrics to European regulators.

00:02:51.840 --> 00:02:57.480
Similar localized data will likely be required before wider deployment in other approved countries.

00:02:58.420 --> 00:03:03.140
The release arrives while the company continues to emphasize the value of the supervised system.

00:03:04.020 --> 00:03:08.600
Official safety data contrasts with a high-profile attention incident the same week.

00:03:09.300 --> 00:03:15.280
A driver was recorded apparently napping while using supervised full self-driving on a California highway.

00:03:15.540 --> 00:03:20.740
The video has renewed questions about the effectiveness of current driver monitoring systems.

00:03:21.340 --> 00:03:26.320
Tesla has stated that its supervised software does not waste driver time during operation.

00:03:27.100 --> 00:03:32.500
The incident occurs as regulators continue to examine attention requirements in partially automated

00:03:32.500 --> 00:03:38.620
vehicles. Attention concerns sit alongside incremental feature rollouts that aim to improve daily

00:03:38.620 --> 00:03:44.720
usability. Tesla owners have shared details about the supervised FSD subscription pricing.

00:03:45.360 --> 00:03:51.420
One mentioned paying $99 per month for the FSD sub when replying to criticism of the feature.

00:03:52.120 --> 00:03:55.960
Another expressed comfort with being luggage while the car handles the driving.

00:03:56.600 --> 00:04:01.280
A third pointed out the $18 monthly charge and noted that the car drives itself,

00:04:01.520 --> 00:04:03.900
which proves great for waiting and parking lots.

00:04:04.620 --> 00:04:09.600
These comments come as the company continues incremental updates to the supervised system.

00:04:10.240 --> 00:04:15.100
The varied pricing references may reflect different subscription tiers or regional offers.

00:04:15.760 --> 00:04:18.960
Listeners can expect more owner feedback as adoption grows.

00:04:19.780 --> 00:04:25.240
Rivians CEO addressed comparisons between their upcoming autonomy features and Tesla's system.

00:04:26.080 --> 00:04:31.300
The point-to-point capability is expected to be very similar to Tesla's FSD this year.

00:04:31.980 --> 00:04:35.860
The comment came during discussions of competitive autonomous driving efforts.

00:04:35.860 --> 00:04:40.460
It positions Rivian as aiming for similar functionality in the near term.

00:04:41.140 --> 00:04:45.520
Tesla's broader testing footprint across states provides a benchmark for such claims.

00:04:46.220 --> 00:04:51.120
The statement arrives amid continued regulatory reviews for unsupervised operation.

00:04:51.920 --> 00:04:55.220
Future updates will clarify how the systems differ in practice.

00:04:56.020 --> 00:05:01.060
Elon Musk commented on potential future evaluations tied to Tesla's autonomy projects.

00:05:01.780 --> 00:05:06.800
He indicated that robo-taxes could contribute up to $5 trillion in value.

00:05:07.320 --> 00:05:12.040
Optimus was projected to reach $25 trillion in valuation impact.

00:05:12.680 --> 00:05:16.860
The statements were shared in the context of ongoing development for both programs.

00:05:17.600 --> 00:05:22.160
They build on the current supervised FSD progress and cybercab testing.

00:05:22.840 --> 00:05:26.940
Such projections highlight the long-term ambitions beyond current vehicle sales.

00:05:27.660 --> 00:05:31.880
Observers will watch how these figures align with actual deployment timelines.

00:05:33.060 --> 00:05:37.280
LM Advisers LLC recently trimmed its stock position in Tesla.

00:05:37.920 --> 00:05:40.960
The move was reported as part of portfolio adjustments.

00:05:41.540 --> 00:05:45.620
A contrast with Goldman Sachs increasing its holdings earlier in the quarter.

00:05:46.360 --> 00:05:51.140
Institutional activity remains mixed as the stock navigates valuation questions.

00:05:51.880 --> 00:05:55.500
The trimming adds the picture of shifting positions among various funds.

00:05:56.060 --> 00:05:58.520
No specific share count was detailed in the report.

00:05:59.160 --> 00:06:02.660
Such actions will be tracked in future filings for broader trends.

00:06:03.600 --> 00:06:07.640
Tesla is preparing to release actually smart summon on the cyber truck.

00:06:08.140 --> 00:06:13.620
The feature will allow the vehicle to navigate parking lots and approach the owner without driver input.

00:06:14.320 --> 00:06:19.260
It follows earlier cyber truck specific software updates that tested large vehicle handling.

00:06:20.160 --> 00:06:24.100
Owners will monitor how the system manages the truck's size and turning radius.

00:06:24.100 --> 00:06:28.740
The rollout comes ahead of broader unsupervised ambitions across the lineup.

00:06:29.500 --> 00:06:33.620
Vehicle specific autonomy features tie into broader navigation refinements.

00:06:34.240 --> 00:06:39.720
The navigation map now displays available parking options directly as drivers approach their destination.

00:06:40.540 --> 00:06:44.320
The change reduces the need to switch screens or consult separate applications.

00:06:44.980 --> 00:06:49.740
It continues earlier refinements aimed at keeping driver attention on the primary display.

00:06:50.540 --> 00:06:54.620
Further map layer additions are expected in upcoming software releases.

00:06:55.240 --> 00:06:58.800
Small UI wins connect to larger software standardization moves.

00:06:59.620 --> 00:07:02.960
Camp mode is now shipping as a standard feature on every new Tesla.

00:07:03.580 --> 00:07:08.400
The over-the-air update enables climate control, lights and media while the vehicle is part.

00:07:09.140 --> 00:07:13.000
It removes the previous paywall and any required configuration steps.

00:07:13.720 --> 00:07:17.400
Tesla highlighted the change with a simple post that included a camping emoji.

00:07:17.400 --> 00:07:21.900
The feature is now available at no extra cost across the entire lineup.

00:07:22.520 --> 00:07:27.120
Customer-facing software polish contrasts with manufacturing compliance issues.

00:07:27.860 --> 00:07:34.400
The Bay Area air quality management district issued 17 violations to the Fremont factory in a single day.

00:07:35.120 --> 00:07:39.920
The citations center on air emissions and permitting requirements at the assembly plant.

00:07:40.600 --> 00:07:45.000
Tesla has not yet outlined corrective steps or any impact on production schedules.

00:07:45.640 --> 00:07:50.080
The factory continues to serve as a key production site for multiple vehicle lines.

00:07:50.620 --> 00:07:55.520
Factory compliance questions lead into supply chain developments that also affect scaling.

00:07:56.340 --> 00:08:01.860
Tesla released the full specification and reference code for its Tesla Transport Protocol on GitHub.

00:08:02.320 --> 00:08:07.340
The company also joined the ultra ethernet consortium to help standardize the protocol.

00:08:08.180 --> 00:08:13.460
Inside Dojo clusters, the protocol operates at layer 2 using standard ethernet switches.

00:08:14.180 --> 00:08:19.820
The design eliminates IP and UDP header processing to reduce latency between training nodes.

00:08:20.620 --> 00:08:25.580
Observers will track whether other organizations adopt the open code in production systems.

00:08:26.240 --> 00:08:30.040
Internal AI infrastructure work links to battery supply chain shifts.

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:35.860
Taiwan's Elise is expanding capacity with connections to Tesla's battery sourcing needs.

00:08:36.640 --> 00:08:40.600
The move underscores Tesla's multi-continent approach to sell procurement.

00:08:41.240 --> 00:08:45.780
Supply decisions now span suppliers across Asia, North America, and Europe.

00:08:46.160 --> 00:08:50.600
The expansion could influence cost and availability for upcoming vehicle models.

00:08:51.100 --> 00:08:55.820
Watch for further supplier updates that clarify the sourcing makes through 2027.

00:08:56.380 --> 00:09:01.320
Supply moves close with real-world ownership data that reinforces cost advantages.

00:09:02.140 --> 00:09:08.060
A UK survey by Rigid ranked the Model 3 as the highest satisfaction car for owners this year.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:13.720
Respondents pointed to low running costs and regular software updates as key factors.

00:09:14.020 --> 00:09:19.620
In the United States, one owner logged 117,000 miles in a Model 3.

00:09:20.320 --> 00:09:24.960
The driver calculated fuel savings far below the cost of an equivalent gasoline sedan.

00:09:25.920 --> 00:09:31.060
Such reports provide Tesla with concrete data points for fleet and regulatory discussions.

00:09:31.820 --> 00:09:35.260
Before we go, keep an eye on June wholesale figures from China,

00:09:35.260 --> 00:09:38.840
and the first European sites using the new foldable superchargers.

00:09:39.320 --> 00:09:41.540
And that's a wrap on today's Tesla news.

00:09:42.260 --> 00:09:49.720
TSLA closed at $406.43, up $7.28, 1.8%.

